// THIS LINE WAS MISSING AND THAT WAS A REAL BUG. The control
// defaults MaxAttachmentSize to 10, so the hint line
// advertised whatever MaxFileSize said while the control
// rejected anything over 10MB with its own "file too large"
// message. A stated limit that is not the enforced limit is
// worse than no limit shown at all.
//
// MB HERE IS DECIMAL, 1,000,000 bytes, per the control's
// documentation. The row and footer size labels in this
// component divide by 1048576, which is binary MiB. The two
// disagree by about 5 percent. Left alone deliberately: file
// managers show binary, upload limits are quoted decimal, and
// changing either would make one of the two lie.
//
// THERE IS STILL A PLATFORM CEILING ABOVE THIS. Reports put
// it near 50MB, with failures well before that on slow
// connections, so raising MaxFileSize past that will produce
