)
// THREE FALLBACKS, AND THE LAST ONE IS THE POINT.
// TypeColors is a TABLE input, so like Style and Colors its
// default never reaches a pasted instance and it arrives
// EMPTY. Both lookups then return blank, and a blank colour
// paints BLACK, which is how a tidy row of coloured tiles
// became a row of black squares with black letters on them.
//
// Coalesce walks: the matching extension, then the row whose
// Ext is default, then a literal neutral grey that cannot
// fail. The literal is what makes the component render
// correctly with TypeColors omitted entirely.
//
// This also replaces the old With / CountRows shape. Coalesce
// already stops at the first non blank, so counting rows to
// decide which branch to take was doing by hand what the
// function does.

Coalesce(
    First(
        Filter(
            cmpFileUpload.TypeColors,
            Lower(Ext) = Lower(Coalesce(ThisItem.Ext, ""))
        )
    ).Text,
    LookUp(cmpFileUpload.TypeColors, Lower(Ext) = "default").Text,
    RGBA(75, 85, 99, 1)
)

